            <ArticleTitle>An asthmatic adolescent with hematuria and hemoptysis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>812-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>When alveolar hemorrhage occurs in association with glomerulonephritis, one of the leading causes is Goodpasture syndrome. We report a case of an adolescent who presented to the emergency department in respiratory distress. Subsequent evaluation was consistent with the diagnosis of Goodpasture syndrome.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
